+- REWORK 05: C-family `##` and `%:%:` handling now produces one canonical complete/reconstructed identifier set used by process/exec, libcurl, Foundation network, Objective-C URL-selector, and Objective-C reflection checks. Five added Clang-backed Objective-C subcases prove both paste spellings reject URL-loading selectors and reflection symbols and that pasted Foundation network classes reject; safe unrelated token paste plus selector/reflection fragments confined to comments and strings remains accepted.
 - CLAIM BOUNDARY: The gate verifies the complete classified repository runtime surface against its enumerated forbidden mechanisms. It is not a general semantic proof for arbitrary future languages; any unclassified file must fail until policy and scanner review.
 - VERIFICATION: Twenty-one focused Python tests include compiler/typechecker/preprocessor-backed regressions for all six re-review 04 bypasses plus the prior C macro, escaped-identifier, function-pointer, token-paste, Swift initializer/typealias, Objective-C selector, and Go import cases. The relay-toolchain CI job now checks out full Git history and has a static regression binding that setting to the provenance audit. Supply-chain/asset audits, manifest tests, relay Go tests/vet, unsigned Swift build, formatting/lint, privacy, diff, full-history local-clone audit, and byte-identical double generation are the handoff gates.
 - BOARD ANOMALY: `task-board validate` exits 0 while reporting the pre-existing `EPIC-260715-2lz67t` stored `to-dev` versus child aggregate `development` mismatch. The task contract forbids weakening validation or falsifying parent dependencies, so the anomaly remains separate from this ready-for-review handoff.
